From 0270d4d7972ac810553f10e6cda979bbe7614929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:36:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Extensions on phones: guards for
 tabs/windows/dialogs/usb/stale actions

Upstream's desktop-Android extension runtime assumes desktop-Android
feature overrides and a window. On phones:
- kLoadAllTabsAtStartup on by default (C++ feature + Java cached flag):
  restored background tabs get WebContents, so the CHECKs in
  tabs_event_router.cc hold and extensions listening to tabs.*/windows.*
  (uBlock Origin etc.) no longer crash-loop at startup with 2+ tabs.
- ExtensionHost::GetJavaScriptDialogManager returns null without a
  top-level window (alert()/confirm() from background pages).
- developerPrivate null-checks the Safety Hub service (incognito).
- WebUSB not offered to extension service workers on phones
  (NOTREACHED in WebUsbServiceImpl).
- Stale action rows (extension reloaded/removed while the menu is open)
  are ignored instead of dereferencing a missing action.
- windows.create on Android 10/11 fails gracefully instead of tripping
  MultiWindowUtils asserts; failed window creation from a background
  page no longer reaches CHECK(browser).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
